p.src:
Fix two points in the plane and represent a curve between them by $y(x)$. Over a short segment, $ds=\sqrt{dx^2+dy^2}
  =dx\sqrt{1+\left(\frac{dy}{dx}\right)^2},$ where the last form assumes $dx>0$. The total length is the functional $S[y]=\int_{x_0}^{x_1}
  \sqrt{1+y'(x)^2}\,dx.$ Square brackets emphasize that $S$ takes an entire function as input. The straight line is selected by $\delta S=0$ under small changes of the curve that leave both endpoints fixed.

