    -\frac{\partial L_{n-1}}{\partial v_{n-1}}
  \right)
  =
  \frac{\partial L_n}{\partial x_n}.$ 左边是一个相邻差商。当 $\epsilon\to0$ 时，折线变成光滑路径，而该商变成时间导数： $\boxed{
  \frac{d}{dt}\left(\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot x}\right)
  =
  \frac{\partial L}{\partial x}}
  .$ 这就是欧拉–拉格朗日方程。

p.src:
Indeed, because $L_{\mathrm{rot}}$ has no explicit time dependence, $\begin{aligned}
    H_{\mathrm{rot}}
    &=\dot X\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot X}
     +\dot Y\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot Y}-L\\
    &=\frac{m}{2}(\dot X^2+\dot Y^2)
     -\frac{m\omega^2}{2}(X^2+Y^2)
  \end{aligned}$ is conserved. It is the rotating-frame Jacobi integral, not the same numerical energy assigned by the inertial observer. Time-dependent coordinate changes need not preserve the numerical form of energy.

